zlib-ng: skip GNU-ld version-script on illumos

Sun ld (illumos /usr/bin/ld, what our gcc defaults to via --with-ld=)
doesn't accept GNU ld's --version-script flag and reports

  ld: fatal: unrecognized option '--version-script'

Sun ld uses mapfile syntax instead (-M file), but the file format is
incompatible with the GNU version-script grammar zlib-ng ships. The
simplest fix is to skip the GNU symbol-versioning machinery on illumos
entirely; the resulting libz-ng.so just doesn't carry symbol versions,
which is fine for our consumers (git, etc.).

The same enclosing `if` block also adds -DHAVE_SYMVER, which is what
gates the use of __attribute__((symver(...))) elsewhere; skip both
together so we don't get unresolved-symbol references at link time.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1284,7 +1284,7 @@ if(BUILD_SHARED_LIBS)
         if(HAVE_NO_INTERPOSITION)
             set_target_properties(zlib PROPERTIES COMPILE_FLAGS "-fno-semantic-interposition")
         endif()
-        if(NOT APPLE AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL AIX)
+        if(NOT APPLE AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL AIX AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL SunOS)
             if(NOT ZLIB_COMPAT)
                 add_definitions(-DHAVE_SYMVER)
             endif()
